WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:02,260
Your family's conditions are so difficult

2
00:00:02,260 --> 00:00:03,980
Don’t live in a dormitory that’s 90 billion years old

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:06,140
I spend two thousand a month to help my grandma.

4
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:08,740
It won’t add any burden to your family, but it will be a little bit

5
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:10,340
But I can also do part-time work at ordinary times

6
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:12,020
This amount can basically be covered.

7
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:13,700
After all, it is for better learning

8
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,260
Success in the postgraduate entrance examination is considered a fortune

9
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,420
Invest in yourself

10
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,940
I would also like to thank Grandma Lin

11
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:19,100
Such a good place

12
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,980
It only costs me 2,000 yuan for rent

13
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:22,660
When I'm fine in the future

14
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:25,060
I’ll cook this for you often

15
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,420
OK OK

16
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,820
You don’t have to do it often

17
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:30,260
You have to work and take the postgraduate entrance examination

18
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:31,620
Too hard

19
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,940
Grandma, just try something new once in a while

20
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,750
Thank you, grandma, grandma

21
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,350
Actually I'm not that good either

22
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:43,190
Studying requires a combination of work and mind

23
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:44,710
I usually read novels

24
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:46,390
There is a suspense writer called Seventh Day.

25
00:00:46,390 --> 00:00:48,820
did you know

26
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:49,980
Eat more food

27
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:52,180
Read less useless idle books

28
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,340
Relax and read a book

29
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:54,940
If you are not tired, who is tired?

30
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:57,140
How can we say Wen Xue’s works are useless?

31
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,460
Didn’t you also like to watch it when you were a kid?

32
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:02,680
There are quite a lot of these kinds of books in your room.

33
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,920
No matter how old you are

34
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:07,840
You're not as talkative as others.

35
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,320
After dinner later

36
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:11,720
You can wash the dishes for this meal.

37
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,920
I won’t say it anymore, okay?
